    <string name="general_guide_intro">BaziKhooneh is a growing collection of familiar multiplayer games. Choose a game from the home screen to see its available modes and its own rules and guide.</string>
    <string name="general_guide_account">Local and bot games do not require an account. One shared account gives you access to online play, invitations, your profile, and match history across every game.</string>
    <string name="general_guide_accessibility">The visual interface and accessibility experience are designed together. Controls have spoken labels and usable touch sizes, and important game events are announced in order for screen readers.</string>
    <string name="guide_rules">Each player has three pieces. First, players take turns placing their pieces on the 3 by 3 board. Forming a complete row, column, or diagonal wins. If nobody wins after all six pieces are placed, select one of your pieces and move it to any empty cell. Movement is not limited to adjacent cells.</string>
    <string name="guide_accessibility">Every board cell announces its row, column, and current piece. After each action, the move and next turn are announced together so screen readers do not miss information.</string>
